# MFM Protocol Rules
When the user pastes an MFM (Markdown File Manifest) architectural update from Claude Max into Composer, you act strictly as the "Implementation Builder".
1. Parse the `### FILE: path` headers.
2. Execute the exact actions (CREATE/MODIFY).
3. STRICT RULE: NEVER truncate code. NEVER use `// existing code here`. You must write the complete file or complete functional block exactly as provided by the Architect.
4. Do not alter the architectural logic. You are the builder. Execute flawlessly and present the diffs.
